3601: \begin{enumerate}
3602: \item \emph{gate implementation soundness}: soundness of an actual automath or
3603: newmath gate implementation beyond the external predicate
3604: $\mathsf{RGS}_{S}(P,L,\Gamma)$;
3605: \item \emph{exact or semantic source import}: exact source theorem statements,
3606: fresh BEDC/Lean rebuilds, axiom-purity, or semantic truth of the imported source
3607: theorems beyond the bounded source-interface rows;
3608: \item \emph{row-frozen package completeness}: extractor completeness for every
3609: possible prose claim in the supplement, or any extension beyond the explicitly
3610: enumerated current-package ledger rows, without adding corresponding rows and
3611: rerunning the finite checks;
3612: \item \emph{artifact semantics}: dynamic Rule110/GroundCompiler validity,
3613: evaluator semantics, or fresh artifact-suite outcomes beyond the submitted
3614: manifest, snapshot, status, and limitation rows; and
3615: \item \emph{semantic theorem-inventory completeness}: proof correctness,
3616: theorem adequacy, semantic proof checking, Lean/BEDC rebuild, or theorem-like
3617: material outside the declared syntactic extractor domain $\mathcal E$.
3618: \end{enumerate}
3619: For each axis $a\in J$, let $B_{a}$ be the finite extension budget required for
3620: that stronger demand by Theorems~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form}
3621: and~\ref{thm:boundary-axis-non-escalation-exactness}, with the row-frozen package
3622: axis using the same normal form applied to the current-package rows of
3623: Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness} and the ledger boundary
3624: of Theorem~\ref{thm:manual-ledger-dependence-boundary}.  Then $c^{+}$ is accepted
3625: by the same finite-record publication interface if and only if every coordinate
3626: in the union $\bigcup_{a\in J}B_a$ is present in the submitted support surface and
3627: passes its assigned gate.  If the unpaid set
3628: \[
3629: M=\{a\in J: B_a\text{ is not fully present with passing assigned gates}\}
3630: \]
3631: is nonempty, then $c^{+}$ has an inclusion-minimal finite bad subrecord whose
3632: projection lies in one of the unpaid axes in $M$, and adding records only on axes
3633: outside $M$ cannot make $c^{+}$ accepted.  Consequently no support coordinate in
3634: one of the five families can be used as a substitute for a missing coordinate in
3635: another family: the record-gate, source-interface, row-frozen ledger,
3636: manifest-witness, and theorem-inventory boundaries are jointly confined by a
3637: finite extension-budget lower bound.
3638: \end{theorem}
3639: 
3640: \begin{proof}
3641: The proof is the bad-record skeleton argument applied simultaneously to the five
3642: listed axes.  Start with the accepted finite certificate
3643: $\mathcal C(c)=(K,\ell,E,H,R,D,B)$ supplied by
3644: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  Since $c^{+}$ is obtained by
3645: adding stronger demands, each added demand is a stronger reading in the preorder
3646: of Definition~\ref{def:stronger-reading-preorder} unless its content is already
3647: record-equivalent to $c$.  Record-equivalent additions have empty budget and may
3648: be deleted from $J$ without changing the claim.  Thus every remaining axis in
3649: $J$ is a genuine strengthening.
3650: 
3651: For each genuine strengthening, Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form}
3652: identifies the necessary and sufficient finite extension tuple
3653: $(\Delta K,\Delta E,\Delta H,\Delta R,\Delta D,\Delta B)$.  Specialising that
3654: normal form gives the five budgets in the statement.  Gate implementation
3655: soundness requires implementation identity, specification, source-state or
3656: version, and a matching implementation-soundness pass row or command-run tuple.
3657: Exact or semantic source import requires exact source text, a formal-rebuild or
3658: equivalent command-run coordinate, or a semantic source-validation coordinate.
3659: Row-frozen package completeness requires new explicit ledger rows and the finite
3660: verifier records that read those rows, because
3661: Theorems~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness} and
3662: \ref{thm:manual-ledger-dependence-boundary} identify only the enumerated ledger
3663: surface.  Artifact semantics requires an evaluator contract, artifact-semantic
3664: pass row, or fresh evaluator command-run tuple tied to the manifest row.  Semantic
3665: theorem-inventory completeness requires a proof-checking, theorem-adequacy,
3666: formal-rebuild, or out-of-domain extractor coordinate; the syntactic extractor of
3667: Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary} pays only
3668: for label coverage inside $\mathcal E$.
3669: 
3670: If every coordinate in $\bigcup_{a\in J}B_a$ is present and each assigned gate
3671: passes, enlarge $\mathcal C(c)$ by adjoining exactly those finite coordinates.
3672: Each clause of Definition~\ref{def:certificate-schema-acceptance-table} then reads
3673: a present coordinate: claim kinds and evidence levels are in the enlarged $K$ and
3674: $\ell$, evidence surfaces in $E$, assigned gate rows in $R$, route or external
3675: boundaries in $H$, discovery/source rows in $D$, and command or limitation data in
3676: $B$.  Theorem~\ref{thm:record-acceptance-exactness} therefore accepts the enlarged
3677: certificate, so $c^{+}$ is accepted at precisely the paid evidence level.
3678: 
3679: Conversely suppose that some axis in $J$ is unpaid.  By the same normal-form
3680: theorem, acceptance of $c^{+}$ would force the missing coordinate of $B_a$ to be
3681: present with its assigned pass row.  Since it is absent or nonpassing, the first
3682: schema clause that reads it fails.  Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton}
3683: then produces an inclusion-minimal bad subrecord: a missing evidence surface,
3684: missing assigned-gate row, missing promotion or external boundary, missing
3685: source/discovery row, or unsupported command-run escalation.  That subrecord is
3686: contained in the finite budget of an unpaid axis, so its projection lies in $M$.
3687: 
3688: Finally, adding records only on axes outside $M$ leaves at least one unpaid
3689: budget $B_a$ with $a\in M$ unchanged.  The same failed schema clause and the same
3690: minimal bad-subrecord classification remain.  Hence cross-axis substitution is
3691: impossible: a source snapshot cannot prove gate implementation soundness, a
3692: manifest row cannot prove artifact semantics without evaluator coordinates, a
3693: theorem-inventory label check cannot prove proof correctness, and a row-frozen
3694: package ledger cannot become semantically complete without fresh rows and checks.
3695: This proves the stated joint confinement and lower bound.
3696: \end{proof}
3697: 
3698: \begin{theorem}[Package-local boundary normal form for the presentation package]
3699: \label{thm:presentation-scoped-boundary-normal-form}
3700: Assume the submitted package is evaluated only through the finite-record
3701: interface of Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  Then every accepted
3702: load-bearing claim using one of the five interface components below has the stated
3703: maximal bounded reading, and every strictly stronger reading has the indicated
3704: unpaid obstruction unless the submitted surface is enlarged by a fresh finite
3705: coordinate and its assigned pass record.
3706: \begin{enumerate}
3707: \item \emph{Publication safety}: the accepted reading is conditional finite-record
3708: safety under the external record-gate-soundness predicate
3709: \(\mathsf{RGS}_{S}(P,L,\Gamma)\).  An implementation-soundness reading of the
3710: record gates is obstructed by a missing implementation-specification,
3711: source-state, and implementation-soundness pass or command-run coordinate.
3712: \item \emph{Imported source interface}: the accepted reading of
3713: Lemma~\ref{lem:source-interface-extraction-correctness} is the path-verified
3714: bounded source-interface record consisting of path, commit, label, line range,
3715: extraction date, bounded summary, and mirror file.  A fresh Lean/BEDC rebuild,
3716: exact source-theorem import, axiom-purity statement, or semantic source-theorem
3717: truth reading is obstructed by a missing formal-source or command-run coordinate.
3718: \item \emph{Finite witnesses}: the accepted reading of
3719: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-witness-manifest-record-interface} is manifest-bounded:
3720: manifest rows, evaluator-facing outcomes explicitly recorded in those rows,
3721: reviewable snapshots, status pass records, and limitation-ledger records.  Dynamic
3722: Rule110/GroundCompiler semantic validation is obstructed by a missing evaluator
3723: contract, artifact-semantic pass row, or fresh evaluator command-run coordinate.
3724: \item \emph{Primary-claim inventory}: the accepted reading of
3725: Proposition~\ref{prop:primary-claim-row-classification} and
3726: Proposition~\ref{prop:primary-inventory-freshness-criterion} is manual
3727: claim-audit completeness plus row-span and certificate-field freshness for the
3728: specific primary source being audited.  A semantic extractor for arbitrary later
3729: prose edits is obstructed by a missing fresh manual audit of the edited primary
3730: source and a missing fresh verifier record for the edited inventory fields.
3731: \item \emph{Theorem inventory}: the accepted reading of
3732: Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary} and
3733: Theorem~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary} is syntactic
3734: environment-label coverage for the declared theorem-like environment domain
3735: \(\mathcal E\).  Proof correctness, theorem adequacy, semantic completeness, Lean
3736: or BEDC rebuild, and artifact validation are obstructed by missing formal-source,
3737: proof-checking, semantic-checking, or artifact-validation coordinates.
3738: \end{enumerate}
3739: Consequently the current package has a sharp finite-record skeleton for the
3740: presentation-only route: the accepted claims are exactly these bounded readings
3741: together with the certificates cited by their statements, and the five stronger
3742: families above cannot be inferred from the manuscript by prose escalation.  This
3743: normal form is package-local: it applies only to packages using the same finite
3744: schema, submitted support-surface convention, dispatch table, and five-component
3745: boundary design, and it asserts no classification theorem for AI-assisted
3746: mathematics pipelines with different schemas or evidence surfaces.
3747: \end{theorem}
3748: 
3749: \begin{proof}
3750: Let \(c\) be an accepted load-bearing claim using one of the five listed interface
3751: components, and let \(\mathcal C(c)=(K,\ell,E,H,R,D,B)\) be its accepted
3752: certificate from Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  By
3753: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-record-certificate-rigidity}, the value of any accepted
3754: consequence is determined by the finite submitted coordinates read by
3755: \(\mathcal C(c)\), the submitted surface \(S\), the ledger \(L\), and the dispatch
3756: table \(\Gamma\).  Hence two surrounding states that agree on those coordinates
3757: but differ in a live gate implementation, source checkout, evaluator run,
3758: primary-prose edit, proof-checker state, or artifact semantics must give the same
3759: accepted certificate and the same rejected bad subrecords.  Any claimed
3760: difference depending on one of those unsubmitted states is therefore not a
3761: consequence of the accepted finite record.
3762: 
3763: For item~1, the statement of Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}
3764: explicitly assumes \(\mathsf{RGS}_{S}(P,L,\Gamma)\) and states that no independent
3765: implementation-soundness, fresh-execution, or semantic-correctness claim about the
3766: gates is inferred without source path, command, source state, environment, exit
3767: code, and log path.  Thus an implementation-soundness upgrade changes the
3768: implementation or command-boundary fields and is governed by
3769: Theorem~\ref{thm:boundary-axis-non-escalation-exactness}.
3770: 
3771: For item~2, Lemma~\ref{lem:source-interface-extraction-correctness} identifies the
3772: complete imported interface as the manually audited path, commit, line range,
3773: bounded summary, extraction date, and mirror file, and
3774: Proposition~\ref{prop:manual-source-interface-non-escalation} proves that exact
3775: source-statement import, rebuild, axiom-purity, and semantic validation require
3776: additional source-statement, formal-build, or command-run coordinates.  Therefore
3777: the path-verified bounded reading is maximal below those upgrades.
3778: 
3779: For item~3, Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-witness-manifest-record-interface} lists the
3780: coordinate set \(\mathcal M_{a_6}\) read for finite-witness claims, and
3781: Corollary~\ref{cor:artifact-semantic-validity-boundary} proves that unbounded
3782: Rule110/GroundCompiler semantics require an evaluator contract, artifact pass
3783: record, or evaluator command-run tuple.  Agreement on \(\mathcal M_{a_6}\) is
3784: therefore sufficient for the accepted manifest-bounded reading and insufficient
3785: for dynamic semantic validation.
3786: 
3787: For item~4, Proposition~\ref{prop:primary-claim-row-classification} is proved by a
3788: finite manual inspection of the current primary-claim rows, while
3789: Proposition~\ref{prop:primary-inventory-freshness-criterion} states the three
3790: conditions needed for an edited source: a fresh manual audit list, live pointers
3791: to submitted certificate surfaces, and evidence levels bounded by those
3792: certificates.  Its command-run paragraph is limited to row-span and
3793: certificate-field freshness.  Thus a later arbitrary prose edit that lacks a new
3794: manual audit or a refreshed verifier record differs in an unsubmitted coordinate
3795: and is rejected as an unclassified-row, stale-pointer, or evidence-level
3796: obstruction.
3797: 
3798: For item~5, Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary}
3799: states that the extractor scans only the five syntactic environment names in
3800: \(\mathcal E\), compares source labels with inventory labels, and does not parse
3801: mathematical statements, check proofs, invoke Lean, consult the daemon, or
3802: validate artifacts.  Theorem~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary} therefore
3803: accepts only obligation-ledger and syntactic label-coverage claims.  Any proof
3804: correctness, adequacy, semantic-completeness, rebuild, or artifact-validation
3805: upgrade changes a finite coordinate outside the extractor tuple and is rejected
3806: until the corresponding formal-source, semantic-checking, or artifact-validation
3807: record is supplied.
3808: 
3809: The five cases exhaust the scoped weak points named in this presentation package
3810: under the stated finite schema and support-surface convention.
3811: In each case, Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form} supplies the
3812: positive extension budget for a genuine upgrade, and
3813: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton} supplies the
3814: inclusion-minimal bad subrecord when that budget is absent.  This proves both the
3815: maximal bounded readings and the non-escalation conclusion.
3816: \end{proof}
3817: \begin{theorem}[Package-local five-axis upgrade obstruction]
3818: \label{thm:five-axis-upgrade-obstruction}
3819: Assume the hypotheses of
3820: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  Let $c$ be an accepted
3821: load-bearing claim in this presentation package, evaluated with this paper's
3822: finite schema, submitted support surface, dispatch table $\Gamma$, and boundary
3823: axis map, whose proof uses at least one of the following bounded interfaces:
3824: \[
3825: \text{record-gate},\quad \text{source-interface},\quad
3826: \text{finite-witness},\quad \text{primary-inventory},\quad
3827: \text{theorem-inventory}.
3828: \]
3829: For each such interface there is a finite upgrade coordinate
3830: \(U_j(c)\subseteq \Delta(c,c^{+})\) with the following exact form.
3831: \begin{enumerate}
3832: \item For a record-gate implementation-soundness reading,
3833: \(U_1(c)\) consists of an implementation object or source state, the gate
3834: specification being checked, and an implementation-soundness pass row or the full
3835: command-run tuple in the boundary field.
3836: \item For an exact or semantic source-theory reading of an imported
3837: source-interface row, \(U_2(c)\) consists of either a submitted extractor/rebuild
3838: artifact for the cited Lean/BEDC source state or exact source-theorem import rows,
3839: together with the assigned pass record.
3840: \item For dynamic artifact or Rule110/GroundCompiler semantic validation,
3841: \(U_3(c)\) consists of an artifact-semantic evaluator contract, the evaluator
3842: input/output surface, and a status pass row or fresh evaluator command-run tuple.
3843: \item For semantic completeness of the primary-claim inventory beyond the twelve
3844: manual rows, \(U_4(c)\) consists of a fresh audit of the edited primary source,
3845: row-span and certificate-field comparison data for that audit, and its verifier
3846: pass record.
3847: \item For proof-dependency assurance or theorem semantic completeness beyond the
3848: declared environment domain $\mathcal E$, \(U_5(c)\) consists of a dependency graph
3849: or semantic proof-review/checker surface, the source-to-output binding for the
3850: covered theorem-like material, and its pass record.
3851: \end{enumerate}
3852: Let $J(c,c^{+})$ be the set of axes on which a proposed stronger reading
3853: $c^{+}$ strengthens $c$.  Then $c^{+}$ is accepted by the same finite-record
3854: safety interface if and only if, for every $j\in J(c,c^{+})$, the submitted
3855: surface contains $U_j(c)$ and the rows in $U_j(c)$ pass the gates assigned by
3856: $\Gamma$.  If any $U_j(c)$ is absent, $c^{+}$ has an inclusion-minimal bad
3857: subrecord on that axis and no combination of the other four bounded interfaces
3858: can discharge the missing coordinate.  Thus the five weak presentation-package
3859: points are not merely warnings inside this schema: each is a separate
3860: finite-budget lower bound for upgrading the main safety theorem beyond its
3861: conditional, path-verified, manifest-bounded, manual-inventory, or
3862: syntactic-inventory reading.  No conclusion is asserted for a system that lacks
3863: these five interfaces or replaces the finite support-surface design by a
3864: different audit schema.
3865: \end{theorem}
3866: 
3867: \begin{proof}
3868: Let \(\mathcal C(c)=(K,\ell,E,H,R,D,B)\) be the certificate accepted for $c$ by
3869: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  The six schema clauses of
3870: Definition~\ref{def:certificate-schema-acceptance-table} read only the finite
3871: fields \(K,\ell,E,H,R,D,B\) and the pass rows assigned by $\Gamma$.  Therefore a
3872: proper stronger reading must differ from $c$ in at least one finite coordinate of
3873: the extension normal form of
3874: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form}; otherwise
3875: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} makes it
3876: record-equivalent to $c$.
3877: 
3878: The five displayed coordinates are obtained by specializing that normal form to
3879: the five scoped interfaces of this package.  A record-gate implementation claim changes the
3880: implementation or command-boundary fields and hence lies in \(\Delta E\),
3881: \(\Delta R\), and \(\Delta B\).  An exact source import, source-theory semantic
3882: claim, or Lean/BEDC rebuild changes the discovery/source-interface surface and
3883: its pass records, hence lies in \(\Delta E\), \(\Delta R\), and \(\Delta D\).  An
3884: artifact-semantic validation changes the artifact evidence surface, the assigned
3885: status/evaluator rows, or the command-boundary field, hence lies in
3886: \(\Delta E\), \(\Delta R\), and \(\Delta B\).  A semantic completeness claim for
3887: the primary inventory changes the manual audit row set and its comparison
3888: records, hence lies in \(\Delta E\), \(\Delta R\), and, when the changed row is a
3889: discovery or source-interface row, \(\Delta D\).  A proof-dependency or semantic
3890: theorem-inventory claim changes the theorem-checking surface and its pass
3891: record, and may also change the command-boundary field; it is not contained in
3892: the syntactic label tuple scanned over $\mathcal E$.  These are exactly the
3893: coordinates listed as \(U_1(c),\ldots,U_5(c)\).
3894: 
3895: If every coordinate \(U_j(c)\) for the strengthened axes is present and passes
3896: the gates assigned by $\Gamma$, adjoining their finite rows to
3897: \(\mathcal C(c)\) gives the enlarged certificate of
3898: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form}.  The six schema clauses
3899: then hold for $c^{+}$, so
3900: Theorem~\ref{thm:record-acceptance-exactness} accepts the stronger reading.
3901: Conversely, if $c^{+}$ is accepted, each changed coordinate must be present and
3902: must satisfy the corresponding schema clause; reading the changed coordinates by
3903: the five cases recovers the required \(U_j(c)\) for every strengthened axis.
3904: 
3905: Suppose finally that one required \(U_j(c)\) is absent.  The first schema clause
3906: that reads a field of that coordinate fails, and
3907: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton} extracts an
3908: inclusion-minimal bad subrecord.  The other bounded interfaces cannot repair this
3909: failure because Theorem~\ref{thm:mixed-interface-overclaim-skeleton} proves
3910: cross-axis substitution impossible: each axis has its own evidence surface, pass
3911: row, discovery/source field, or command-boundary field.  Hence the missing
3912: upgrade coordinate is a genuine finite-budget lower bound, not a prose boundary
3913: that can be discharged by relabelling another record.\end{proof}
3914: 
3915: Together, Theorem~\ref{thm:presentation-scoped-boundary-normal-form} and
3916: Theorem~\ref{thm:five-axis-upgrade-obstruction} are the supplement's bounded
3917: replacement for a stronger article-level claim.  They keep the headline safety
3918: theorem conditional on record-gate soundness, identify the manual/path-verified
3919: status of the imported source interface, confine finite-witness rows to bounded
3920: artifact evidence, confine the primary inventory to the twelve audited rows, and
3921: confine the theorem inventory to syntactic labelled-environment coverage.  Any
3922: future paper that wants unconditional gate implementation soundness, complete
3923: source-theory extraction, dynamic artifact validation, semantic primary-claim
3924: extraction, or proof-dependency assurance must add precisely the corresponding
3925: finite upgrade coordinate above.
3926: 
3927: \begin{theorem}[Current package-local boundary skeleton and non-gluing lower bound]
3928: \label{thm:current-boundary-skeleton-non-gluing}
3929: Assume the support-surface hypotheses used by the current-package instantiation,
3930: including the six-row state $P^{+}_{6}$ of
3931: Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness}, the finite-script
3932: projection records of
3933: Theorem~\ref{thm:concrete-finite-script-implementation-soundness}, the
3934: bounded source-interface certificate of
3935: Theorem~\ref{thm:bounded-source-interface-maximality}, the
3936: manifest-bounded artifact coordinate $\mathcal M_{a_6}$ of
3937: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-witness-manifest-record-interface}, and the syntactic
3938: theorem-environment domain $\mathcal E$ of
3939: Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary}.  Let
3940: $F_{\mathrm{cur}}$ be the finite union of those submitted coordinates together
3941: with the finite record-gate surface used by
3942: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  Then the maximal information
3943: about the current package determined by $F_{\mathrm{cur}}$ is exactly the
3944: following six-coordinate skeleton.  The word ``current'' is load-bearing: the
3945: claim is only about this presentation package with this finite schema and this
3946: support-surface design, and it does not classify packages with different gate
3947: interfaces, artifact semantics, theorem inventories, or venue workflows.
3948: \begin{enumerate}
3949: \item The publication-safety coordinate is conditional finite-record
3950: non-escalation under the explicit predicate
3951: $\mathsf{RGS}_{S}(P,L,\Gamma)$; it is not independent gate implementation
3952: soundness, fresh daemon execution, proof-assistant correctness, artifact
3953: semantics, or venue acceptance.
3954: \item The finite-script coordinate is projection soundness for the printed
3955: finite predicates on the parsed finite input records of the named scripts; it is
3956: not end-to-end correctness of the Python implementation, filesystem model,
3957: runtime, verifier source, or external gate semantics.
3958: \item The imported-source coordinate is the bounded source-interface certificate:
3959: source path, pinned commit, sixteen labels, line ranges, bounded summaries,
3960: table/JSON equality, manifest agreement, snapshot digest and line count, and
3961: label containment in the bundled snapshot.  It is not exact source theorem import,
3962: public byte equality, Lean/BEDC rebuild success, axiom purity, marker correctness,
3963: or semantic truth of the imported discovery-gate statements.
3964: \item The current-package certificate coordinate is the row-frozen six-row map
3965: for $a_1,\ldots,a_6$ and the path-verified instantiation that cites those rows.
3966: Theorem-environment scope coverage is supplied, when cited, only by the separate
3967: Stage-A theorem-inventory/extractor coordinate, not by completeness of the
3968: six-row certificate map for every theorem-like environment.
3969: \item The finite-witness coordinate is the manifest-bounded row $a_6$ interface
3970: $\mathcal M_{a_6}$; it is not unbounded Rule110/GroundCompiler semantic
3971: validity or fresh dynamic evaluator validation.
3972: \item The theorem-inventory coordinate is syntactic label coverage for labelled
3973: environments in the declared domain $\mathcal E$; it is not semantic proof
3974: completeness, proof-dependency assurance, Lean/BEDC rebuild, or artifact
3975: validation.
3976: \end{enumerate}
3977: Moreover these six coordinates do not glue into any stronger conclusion.  For
3978: any proposed strengthened reading $c^{+}$ that changes a nonempty set $J$ of the
3979: six axes, acceptance of $c^{+}$ in the finite-record schema requires the product
3980: of the corresponding finite upgrade budgets: the gate-audit tuple of
3981: Theorem~\ref{thm:assigned-gate-soundness-audit-boundary}, the implementation
3982: budget of Theorem~\ref{thm:concrete-finite-script-implementation-soundness}, the
3983: source semantic-completeness budget of
3984: Theorem~\ref{thm:source-interface-semantic-completeness-obstruction}, the
3985: row-extension budget of Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness}
3986: and Corollary~\ref{cor:row-frozen-current-package-invariance}, the artifact
3987: semantic budget of Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-witness-manifest-record-interface}, and
3988: the proof/semantic theorem-inventory budget of
3989: Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary}, for the
3990: axes in $J$.  If any coordinate in this product budget is absent, the obstruction
3991: is an inclusion-minimal bad subrecord on that unpaid axis, and agreement on all
3992: other coordinates of $F_{\mathrm{cur}}$ cannot repair it.  Thus the current
3993: support surface satisfies a no-subsidy lower bound: a finite-script exit-code row
3994: cannot prove the semantic correctness of the gate it projects, a source-interface
3995: digest cannot prove gate implementation soundness, and a row-frozen package
3996: certificate cannot prove semantic truth of all primary prose or exact imported
3997: source theorem statements.
3998: \end{theorem}
3999: 
4000: \begin{proof}
4001: Each item is a specialization of a labelled theorem already in the finite-record
4002: chain, but the point here is the joint skeleton.  Item~1 is exactly the
4003: conditional hypothesis and boundary of
4004: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}: the theorem reads the submitted
4005: record surface, ledger, dispatch table, and certificate schema, and its statement
4006: excludes unrecorded implementation, execution, semantic, artifact, and venue
4007: claims.  Item~2 follows from
4008: Theorem~\ref{thm:concrete-finite-script-implementation-soundness}, whose proof
4009: identifies the finite input projection for each named script and proves only the
4010: corresponding printed predicate on that projection.  Item~3 is the maximality
4011: statement of Theorem~\ref{thm:bounded-source-interface-maximality}, sharpened by
4012: Theorem~\ref{thm:source-interface-semantic-completeness-obstruction}: the current
4013: record imports bounded rows and finite equality/containment facts, not exact or
4014: semantic source truth.  Item~4 follows from
4015: Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness} and
4016: Corollary~\ref{cor:current-package-path-verified-instantiation}: those results
4017: read the selected six rows $a_1,\ldots,a_6$ and the path catalogue fixed by the
4018: current support surface.  They do not read the semantic content of every
4019: theorem-like environment; syntactic theorem-environment coverage is introduced
4020: separately by
4021: Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary} and
4022: bounded by Theorem~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary}.  Item~5 is the
4023: manifest-record invariance statement proved in
4024: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-witness-manifest-record-interface} and sharpened in
4025: Corollary~\ref{cor:artifact-semantic-validity-boundary}.  Item~6 is the exact
4026: input/output boundary of
4027: Theorem~\ref{thm:deterministic-theorem-environment-extractor-boundary} together
4028: with the semantic separation in
4029: Theorem~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary}.
4030: 
4031: It remains to prove non-gluing.  Let two possible ambient states agree on
4032: $F_{\mathrm{cur}}$ and differ only in one unsubmitted fact, such as live gate
4033: implementation correctness, verifier-source correctness beyond the parsed finite
4034: projection, exact or semantic source truth beyond the bounded imported-source
4035: rows, a certificate row outside $a_1,\ldots,a_6$, dynamic artifact semantics, or
4036: proof completeness beyond the syntactic extractor domain.  By
4037: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}, the finite verifier
4038: and certificate constructor return the same accepted certificates and the same
4039: bad-subrecord reports on these two states.  Hence any assertion whose truth
4040: changes between them is not determined by the current finite record.  Making a
4041: changed assertion load-bearing is exactly the positive-budget case of
4042: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form}; the six boundary theorems
4043: listed in the statement identify the component-wise coordinates of that budget.
4044: If one component of the product budget is absent,
4045: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton} returns an
4046: inclusion-minimal bad subrecord, and
4047: Theorem~\ref{thm:mixed-interface-overclaim-skeleton} rules out substituting pass
4048: records from another axis.  Therefore the six bounded current-package
4049: coordinates remain separate lower bounds inside this package-local schema, and
4050: their union does not certify any of the stronger readings listed in the
4051: statement.\end{proof}
4052: 
4053: For reviewer reproducibility, the constructor and extractor used in
4054: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface} can be written as the following
4055: finite algorithms.  The constructor \(\mathsf{Cert}_{\Gamma}\) reads, in order,
4056: the claim-kind coordinates from the acceptance entry, the declared evidence level,
4057: the cited submitted surfaces, the pass rows assigned by \(\Gamma\), the route
4058: promotion field, the pinned discovery rows when the kind set contains discovery,
4059: and the command-boundary field.  The bad-record extractor \(\mathsf{Bad}_{\Gamma}\)
4060: applies the six schema predicates in the order of
4061: Theorem~\ref{thm:verifier-input-output-contract} and returns the fields read by
4062: the first false predicate.  Thus positive certificates and negative certificates
4063: are built from the same finite coordinates; neither construction consults live
4064: daemon state, proof-assistant semantics, artifact semantics, or venue state.
4065: 
4066: \begin{proposition}[Certificate constructor and bad-subrecord extractor]
4067: \label{prop:certificate-constructor-bad-subrecord-extractor}
4068: Assume the four finite-record hypotheses of
4069: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  For every ledger row \(c\) there
4070: is a deterministic partial constructor
4071: \[
4072: \mathsf{Cert}_{\Gamma}(c)=(K,\ell,E,H,R,D,B)
4073: \]
4074: and a deterministic extractor \(\mathsf{Bad}_{\Gamma}(c)\) with the following
4075: properties.
4076: \begin{enumerate}
4077: \item \(\mathsf{Cert}_{\Gamma}(c)\) is defined and accepted if and only if the
4078: six-clause predicate \(\mathsf{Acc}_{\Gamma}(c,\mathsf{Cert}_{\Gamma}(c))\) holds.
4079: \item If \(\mathsf{Cert}_{\Gamma}(c)\) is rejected, then
4080: \(\mathsf{Bad}_{\Gamma}(c)\) is an inclusion-minimal finite bad subrecord of one
4081: of the five obstruction skeletons in
4082: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton}: missing submitted
4083: evidence, missing assigned gate record, missing route or external decision field,
4084: missing pinned discovery row, or unsupported command-run boundary.
4085: \item For every properly stronger reading \(c^{+}\) of an accepted row, the same
4086: extractor rejects \(c^{+}\) exactly at the first unpaid positive extension
4087: coordinate of Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form}; if no such
4088: coordinate is added, \(c^{+}\) is not distinct from \(c\) in the finite-record
4089: preorder.
4090: \end{enumerate}
4091: Consequently the publication-safety theorem has both a positive certificate
4092: construction algorithm and a negative bad-subrecord extraction algorithm, each
4093: bounded by the submitted schema fields.
4094: \end{proposition}
4095: 
